      "author_association": "MEMBER",
      "body": "> I could imagine benefits to compiler diversity like ensuring is more portable, or finding bugs missed by other compilers, or allowing more developer tools to be used.\r\n\r\nGood point. I guess the only portability issues or bugs were found by using the msSTL, so using clang+msSTL should be fine. If there are real bugs found by msvc (or tools that only work with msvc), it would be good to list them in this brainstorming issue. Otherwise, the reasoning seems recursive, to write portable code to support msvc, for the only reason that msvc can be supported.",
      "user": {
